Z||000000||Ed||03-25-2000||01:44 PM||||Thinking about replacing the seat covers. <P>Mike's leather is about the same price as the Fiero Store's cloth.  <P>1. Are both good quality?<P>2. Pros and cons on cloth v. leather. (P.S., I live in California so cold seats are not a consideration.  Hot seats are!)  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||03-25-2000||03:21 PM||||I have Mr. Mikes leather seats. They are great! Takes about an hour to install each seat. The video is very good and makes the job easy. Since the cost is the same basically I'd go leather!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image09.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-25-2000||03:31 PM||||Those are nice Oreif, you did a good job, and passed on a good deal (lol)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. How do they feel? I bet the leather smeels good too!!!.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||03-25-2000||09:33 PM||||The seats feel very comfortable. When you install the leather seats Mr. Mike gives you some extra foam for the bottom and some cotton wadding for the bolsters. In fact everything you need to do the seats is included! It comes with 2 hogring tools, a large bag of hogrings, Foam padding, cotton wadding, razor blades, spray Glue, and a very detailed video. I am very happy with the quality of the seats. I know a few other people who have had them for a couple of years and they still look new.||||reg||1
